# Rust build artifacts.
#
# `**/target/` (not just `/target`) is deliberate: the vendored crate under
# `vendor/playwright-rs/` builds its own `target/` (~650 MB). A root-anchored `/target` does NOT
# match it, so in a standalone repo `git add -A` would stage the whole thing. Keep both patterns.
/target
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Prebuilt engine binaries. These are release artifacts (tens of MB) that are published via GitHub
# Releases / ghcr, never committed — a binary blob in git history cannot be removed after a push.
.fleet-engine-*
writ-agent-fleet
writ-agentd

# Local runtime logs (see RECORDER_LOG_FILE) — never commit; they leak local
# paths, gateway-discovery attempts, and driver stack traces.
recorder.log*

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local SQLCipher database + WAL/SHM siblings, and the vault key. Never committable.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db-journal
vault.key

# OS cruft
.DS_Store

# Logs
*.log
